    {
      "id": "8d9e5c0aa6e222cd48b34a3a0ab14efb74d8c866",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1118087618,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I wouldn't bother. There isn't any kind of domain registry, any string is a valid domain name (within reason) and the ones in `ws_log_defs.h` are just a small subset.\n\nI think if a developer needs them they probably already know what to look for. At most point them to that header file.",
